            <ArticleTitle>Intramural esophageal bronchogenic cysts.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>69-71</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492310394465</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Bronchogenic cysts are most frequently located in the middle mediastinum near the carina. Esophageal bronchogenic cysts are extremely rare. An intramural esophageal bronchogenic cyst was successfully resected from a 51-year-old man.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
